version: 2.0.0
description: |
  Integration tests for the paradigm CLI. First tests/ file added in v5.37.12
  as regression protection for the fail-closed portal.yaml auth-bypass class
  (see docs/private/plans/portal-yaml-release-split.md).
components:
  plugin-launch-windows-tests:
    description: |
      PR #63 cross-OS suites, run on windows-latest and ubuntu-latest by
      .github/workflows/paradigm-plugin-windows.yml. plugin-mcp-launch.test.ts
      drives #paradigm-mcp-launch with one stub npx (npx-stub.cjs) that behaves
      like npm 11 per OS (devEngines walk-up, --script-shell / default shell
      looked up on the built PATH, ancestors' node_modules/.bin first, cmd
      /d /s /c verbatim); on Windows the launcher starts it as npx-cli.js beside
      a node.exe copied into a path with spaces, so --call quoting goes through
      real cmd.exe. Windows-only cases: no npx-cli.js beside node, % ^ !
      refused, npx folder under %TEMP%, package beside the .cmd shim. POSIX-only
      cases (skipIf, with reasons): owner/mode bits, symlinks, sticky /tmp.
      hooks-missing-cli.test.ts runs the hooks through Git Bash on Windows
      (src/test-shell-utils.ts). e2e/plugin-mcp-launch-e2e.mjs: real npx, the
      published @a-company/paradigm pinned through a temp plugin copy
      (E2E_VERSION), devEngines pnpm/onFail error and planted node/sh/cmd shims
      above the npx folder; expects an MCP initialize reply and no marker.
    type: test
    anchors:
      - plugin-mcp-launch.test.ts
      - hooks-missing-cli.test.ts
      - e2e/plugin-mcp-launch-e2e.mjs
    components:
      - '#paradigm-mcp-launch'
      - '#paradigm-resolve'
    tags:
      - test
      - windows
      - plugin
  portal-compliance-tests:
    description: Regression suite covering the 5 auth-bypass scenarios (A-E) from the 2026-04-22 security audit — prefix mismatch, duplicate-key, Gate[] Array shape, stop-hook exit propagation, valid-portal regression.
    type: test
    anchors:
      - portal-compliance.test.ts:1-400
    tags:
      - test
      - regression
      - portal
      - security
